<p>
    <strong>Blazor Atoms</strong> is a family of small, self-contained Blazor component libraries.
    Each library ships as its own NuGet package with ~zero third-party dependencies: take one
    component, one library, or several, and it just works. No umbrella package, no global theme
    provider, no <code>builder.Services.Add…()</code> registration, no <code>&lt;script&gt;</code>
    tag to wire up.
</p>

<p>
    Every component is plain Blazor plus inline SVG/CSS — themeable through CSS custom properties,
    crisp at any zoom, animatable in pure CSS. JavaScript is used only where a browser primitive
    truly needs it, and always self-loads invisibly to the consumer. The same markup runs unchanged
    in Server, WebAssembly and Auto — which is what these three sibling demo apps exist to prove.
</p>

